  "summary": "Calls SHA256AutoDetect during the startup initialization of bitcoin-util, bitcoin-tx, and bitcoin-wallet. This enables hardware-accelerated SHA-256 implementations on supported CPU architectures instead of falling back to generic software hashing.",
  "problem": "Standalone CLI utilities do not initialize kernel::Context, which is where SHA-256 hardware acceleration detection normally runs. As a result, operations like bitcoin-util grind, batch transaction signing in bitcoin-tx, and wallet operations run hashing routines on the slower generic fallback implementation.",
